  "tagline": "The original SQL-on-Hadoop warehouse, now mostly valued for its Metastore and Iceberg support.",
  "description": "Apache Hive brought SQL to Hadoop at Facebook in 2008: HiveQL compiled to MapReduce, later Tez, over files in HDFS. Hive 4.x runs on Tez with LLAP caching, ACID ORC tables, materialized views with query rewrite and first-class Iceberg tables, and requires JDK 21 from 4.2. Its most enduring piece is the Hive Metastore, still the catalog behind countless Spark, Trino and Impala deployments, now with an Iceberg REST catalog. New projects rarely choose Hive as the query engine, but it remains embedded in Hadoop-era estates.",
